    rprtString: "Tri45.IsInShapeProject_dbg((8.58, 0.13, 4.43))\n{\n|\tflattened
      pos to: '(8.58, 0.00, 4.43)'...\n|\tFirst checking each edge.DoesPositionLieOnEdge()...\n|\tapparently
      all edge checks failed. Checking if position is in triangular area created
      by verts...\n|\tfound that position IS in area. Proceeding...\n|\tthere IS
      slope. This means that surface hit must be calculated with trig...\n|\tnote:
      V_PlaneFaceNormal: '(0.00, 0.77, -0.64)'...\n|\tFirst, getting floor vert index...\n|\tdetermined
      index to be: '1'...\n|\tfirst using edge projection method to help calculate
      angle A...\n|\tEdge[45][1].DoesProjectionIntersectEdge_dbg(start: '(11.22,
      0.00, 4.38)', dest: '(8.58, 0.00, 4.43)', checkIfOriginIsOnEdge: 'False')\n|\t{\n|\t|\t6/18/2026
      9:01:36 AM\n|\t|\tNote: prjction nrml: '(0.00, 1.00, 0.00)'...\n|\t|\tusing
      prjctOrigin_Flat: '(11.22, 0.00, 4.38)', and prjctDest_Flat: '(8.58, 0.00,
      4.43)'...\n|\t|\tusing v_prjct_flat: '(-1.00, 0.00, 0.02)', and v_originToStart_flat:
      '(-1.00, 0.00, 0.07)', v_originToEnd_flat: '(-1.00, 0.00, 0.00)'...\n|\t|\tInclusive/parallel
      checks either not directed, or didn't work. Continuing...\n|\t|\tTrying angular
      short-circuit test...\n|\t|\tNo short-circuits. This means we can project a
      position via trigonometry. Proceeding...\n|\t|\tcalculated lenA: '0.9114014'...\n|\t|\tthis
      edge is NOT flat. Need to continue trigonometric calculation...\n|\t|\tcalculated
      lenB: '0.91668'...\n|\t|\tcalculated outpos: '[t45v-1e1_pos(7.74, 0.05, 4.44)]'.
      Now returning true...\n|\t} <-end of DoesProjectionIntersectEdge_dbg()\n|\tedge
      operation succesful. Got edge hit: '[t45v-1e1_pos(7.74, 0.05, 4.44)]'. Now
      using to calculate angleA...\n|\tnote: vert1 is at '(11.22, 0.00, 4.38)'...\n|\tgot
      lenB: '2.636711' angA: '0.8508785', angC: '89.14912', lenC: '2.63642'...\n|\tCreated
      surface hit: '[t45v-1e-1_pos(8.58, 0.04, 4.43)]'...\n|\treturning true...\n}\n"
